    "verdict": "SEVERITY NOT MANIPULATED IN THE MEASURED QUANTITY: realised AoI has the same median (60 s) and same p90 at every nominal level, and is censored at the 60 s cap in 81.0% of exposed decisions. Tunnel transit time, not the nominal outage duration, sets the staleness a decision actually sees, and the observation encoding cannot represent anything past the cap. The {5,15,30,60} s ladder therefore collapses to a single degraded condition. Flat DEF and WAMSN across levels is the expected consequence of an unmanipulated factor and is NOT evidence about severity; the defensible contrast is binary clean vs degraded."
